  {
    "text": "\n29\n\nT H E U L T I M A T E A N A B O L I C C O O K B O O K 2 . 0\n\nDirections\n1.\nIn a bowl, whisk the egg whites well. Add all the remaining\ningredients (except for the cheese) and mix well.\n2.\nHeat the stove to medium heat. Using a nonstick skillet, spray with\ncooking spray then add the egg mixture and cook on one side for\n3 minutes or until the egg whites are partially cooked.\n3.\nAdd half the cheese and fold over in half and cook for 2 min on\nlow heat.\n4.\nThen when ready, flip, turn or roll the omelette over and cook for\nan additional 2 minutes with remaining cheese slices on top to\nmelt.\n5.\nOnce it is fully cooked, serve with salsa on top or on the side.\nP R E P T I M E\nR E A D Y I N\n15 MINUTES\n20 MINUTES\nIngredients\nM A K E S 2 S E R V I N G S\n480g (2 cups) egg whites \n100g lean deli ham, diced\n1 serving veggies up to 100 calories \n(bell peppers, spinach, tomatoes, \nyellow onions)\n4 slices (or 76g shredded) fat-free \ncheese (120 calories)\nSalt & Pepper to taste\n4 tbsp of your favorite salsa OR 2 \ntbsp no sugar-added ketchup\nN U T R I T I O N\nP E R S E R V I N G\nC A L O R I E S\n2 9 5\nF A T ( G )\n2\nC A R B S ( G )\n2 2\nF I B E R ( G )\n5\nP R O T E I N ( G )\n4 4\nHam & Cheese Omelette\nG L U T E N - F R E E",
