    "text": "\n56\n\nT H E U L T I M A T E A N A B O L I C C O O K B O O K 2 . 0\n\nPumpkin Protein Muffins\nDirections\n1.\nPreheat the oven to 350°F (177°C). Place cupcake liners in a\nmuffin tin and spray them with cooking spray.\n2.\nIn a large bowl, mix all the dry ingredients together well. In a\nseparate bowl, mix all the rest of the ingredients together. Add\nthe wet ingredients to the dry ingredient and mix well until\neverything is incorporated.\n3.\nFill the cupcake liners about ¾ full of the batter. Bake in the oven\nfor 20 minutes or until a toothpick comes out clean.\n4.\nRemove from the oven and allow to cool down for at least 20\nminutes before serving.\nP R E P T I M E\nR E A D Y I N\n15 MINUTES\n40 MINUTES\nIngredients\nM A K E S 8 M U F F I N S\n165g (5 scoops) vanilla protein \npowder\n32g (~¼ cup) coconut flour\n64g erythritol or ~7 packets \nsweetener\n225g (1 cup) pumpkin purée\n120g (½ cup) egg whites\n2 tsp pumpkin pie spice\n20g (4 tsp) baking powder\n½ tsp salt\n5g (1 tsp) vanilla extract\nV E G E T A R I A N\nG L U T E N - F R E E\nT O T A L\nN U T R I T I O N\nC A L O R I E S\n9 3 0\nF A T ( G )\n3 6\nC A R B S ( G )\n5 7\nF I B E R ( G )\n1 6\nP R O T E I N ( G )\n1 4 6\nP R O T E I N ( G )\n1 8\nN U T R I T I O N\nP E R M U F F I N\nC A L O R I E S\n1 2 0\nF A T ( G )\n5\nC A R B S ( G )\n7\nF I B E R ( G )\n2",
