    "text": "\n71\n\nT H E U L T I M A T E A N A B O L I C C O O K B O O K 2 . 0\n\nTriple-Stack Grilled\nEgg & Cheese French Toast\nDirections\n1.\nWhisk the eggs and egg whites in a bowl until the mixture is\nfluffy.\n2.\nHeat a non-stick pan over medium/low heat. Spray with cooking\nspray for one second.\n3.\nPour egg mixture on pan.\n4.\nPlace bread slices on the pan for 15 seconds then flip.\n5.\nCook for a few minutes until the egg mixture is cooked.\nFlip again and cook until the egg is cooked. Then, fold any\nremaining egg mixture onto the bread slices, and place cheese\non top of each slice of bread.\n6.\nPlace the triple-stack sandwich onto a plate and eat with a fork\nand knife, and any condiments you desire.\nN U T R I T I O N\nP E R S E R V I N G\nC A L O R I E S\n6 7 0\nF A T ( G )\n1 1\nC A R B S ( G )\n5 7\nF I B E R ( G )\n2\nP R O T E I N ( G )\n7 5\nR E A D Y I N\n10 MINUTES\nV E G E T A R I A N\nIngredients\nM A K E S 1 S A N D W I C H\n375g (1½ cups) egg whites\n2 whole eggs\n3 slices regular ass bread (240 \ncalories)\n3 slices (or 57g shredded) fat-free \ncheese (60 calories)\nSalt & pepper to taste\nCooking spray\nOptional: \n45g (3 tbsp) sugar-free ketchup (add \n30 calories) OR condiment of choice\nC L I C K H E R E T O \nP U R C H A S E F A T - F R E E \nC H E E S E\nP R E P T I M E\n5 MINUTES",
