    "text": "\nSIDE DISHES\n119\n\nT H E U L T I M A T E A N A B O L I C C O O K B O O K 2 . 0\n\nCauliflower Mashed Potatoes\nDirections\n1.\t Boil 4 liters (or 4 quarts) of water with salt over high heat. Once \nwater starts to boil, reduce heat to medium to bring the water to \na simmer. Add the potatoes and leave in pot until fully cooked \nthrough. Drain in a colander and add to Ninja blender.\n2.\t Separately, cook the cauliflower in a boiling pot of water. Drain in \na colander and add to Ninja blender.\n3.\t Add baking powder, spices, half of the fat-free sour cream, and \nguar gum to Ninja blender and pulse blend until smooth.\n4.\t Serve with the remaining fat-free sour cream and any preferred \nspices and garnish.\nN U T R I T I O N\nP E R S E R V I N G\nC A L O R I E S\n1 5 0\nF A T ( G )\n0\nC A R B S ( G )\n3 3\nF I B E R ( G )\n8\nP R O T E I N ( G )\n5\nP R E P T I M E\nR E A D Y I N\n10 MINUTES\n30 MINUTES\nIngredients\nM A K E S 8 S E R V I N G S\n900g (2 lbs or ~6 medium) potatoes\n900g (2 lbs) cauliflower florets\n230g (1 cup) fat-free sour cream\n9g (3 tsp) guar/xanthan gum \n8g (2 tsp) baking powder\nSpices to taste\nSalt\nOptional garnish: \n1 tbsp chives or scallions, diced\nV E G E T A R I A N\nG L U T E N - F R E E\n“ L I T E ” V E R S I O N S U B S T I T U T I O N S\n450g (1 lb) potatoes instead of 900g (2 lbs)\n450g (1 lb) cauliflower florets instead of 900g (2 lbs)\n6g (2 tsp) guar/xanthan gum instead of 3 tsp\n8g (2 tsp) baking powder (makes it thicker)\nC A L O R I E S\nC A R B S ( G )\nF A T ( G )\nF I B E R ( G )\nP R O T E I N ( G )\n9 0\n1 9\n0\n4\n3",
