    "text": "\n132\n\nT H E U L T I M A T E A N A B O L I C C O O K B O O K 2 . 0\n\nCinnamon Raisin Squares \nDirections\n1.\t Preheat the oven to 325°F (163°C).\n2.\t Combine all wet ingredients into a bowl and whisk and set aside.\n3.\t In a separate large bowl, combine all dry ingredients and stir, then \nadd wet ingredients and stir until smooth consistency.\n4.\t Spray a loaf pan with cooking spray. Pour the batter into the loaf \npan and bake for 25-30 minutes or until a toothpick comes out \nclean.\nP R E P T I M E\nR E A D Y I N\n15 MINUTES\n40 MINUTES\nIngredients\nM A K E S 1 2 C O O K I E S\n180g (¾ cup) egg whites\n570g (2⅓ cup) unsweetened apple \nsauce\n24 packets (1 cup) sweetener \n300g (9 scoops) cinnamon or vanilla \nprotein powder\n120g raisins\n7.5g (1½ tsp) baking powder\n~ 4g (¾ tsp) baking soda\n12g (2 tbsp) cinnamon\n~ 4g (¾ tsp) nutmeg \nV E G E T A R I A N\nG L U T E N - F R E E\nN U T R I T I O N\nP E R B A T C H\nC A L O R I E S\n1 8 7 0\nF A T ( G )\n2 0\nC A R B S ( G )\n1 8 8\nF I B E R ( G )\n1 1\nP R O T E I N ( G )\n2 5 0\nP R O T E I N ( G )\n2 1\nN U T R I T I O N\nP E R S E R V I N G\nC A L O R I E S\n1 5 5\nF A T ( G )\n2\nC A R B S ( G )\n1 6\nF I B E R ( G )\n1",
