    "text": "\n153\n\nT H E U L T I M A T E A N A B O L I C C O O K B O O K 2 . 0\n\nBanana Chocolate Protein \nDonuts\nDirections\n1.\t Preheat the oven to 350°F (177°C)\n2.\t Add the banana and yogurt in a blender and blend till smooth.\n3.\t Add in the rest of the ingredients and blend again until everything \nis well mixed.\n4.\t Spray a donut pan with cooking spray. Fill the donut pan ½ - ¾ \nfull and bake for approximately 10 minutes.\n5.\t Once done, let cool for approximately 1 minute, take the \ndoughnuts out of the molds and let them cool on a wire rack. \nP R E P T I M E\nR E A D Y I N\n20 MINUTES\n40 MINUTES\nIngredients\nM A K E S 4 S E R V I N G S\n220g (2 servings) banana \n125g (½ cup) 0% fat Greek yogurt \n180g (¾ cup) egg whites \n95g (~¾ cup) flour of choice \n132g (4 scoops) chocolate protein \npowder  \n5g (1 tsp) baking soda \n4g (1 tsp) baking powder \n5g (1 tsp) vanilla extract \nV E G E T A R I A N\nG L U T E N - F R E E\nT O T A L\nN U T R I T I O N\nC A L O R I E S\n1 3 5 0\nF A T ( G )\n1 0\nC A R B S ( G )\n1 6 8\nF I B E R ( G )\n1 1\nP R O T E I N ( G )\n1 4 7\nP R O T E I N ( G )\n3 7\nN U T R I T I O N\nP E R S E R V I N G\nC A L O R I E S\n3 2 5\nF A T ( G )\n3\nC A R B S ( G )\n4 2\nF I B E R ( G )\n3",
