    "text": "\n182\n\nT H E U L T I M A T E A N A B O L I C C O O K B O O K 2 . 0\n\nDirections\n1.\t Add all ingredients to a blender. Pulse blend on medium-high \nspeed until there is a smooth consistency. You will likely need to \ntake a spoon and push the ingredients down a few times. Note \nthat the more casein protein is used, the thicker the pudding will \nbe.\n2.\t Remove pudding from blender and transfer across 4 popsicle \ntrays. Transfer to a freezer.\n3.\t Wait a few hours, and pop out the proteinsicles from the tray \nwhen you are ready to have a delicious frozen treat!\nP R E P T I M E\nR E A D Y I N\n20 MINUTES\n2.5 HOURS\nIngredients\nM A K E S 1 B A T C H ( A P P R O X . \n4 M E D I U M S E R V I N G S )\n240ml (1 cup) unsweetened almond \nmilk\n116g (3½) scoops chocolate peanut \nbutter whey protein powder\n300g frozen strawberries (1 serving)\n3g (1 tsp) guar/xanthan gum\n1 package fat-free Jell-O chocolate \npudding (140 calories)\n125g (½ cup) 0% fat Greek yogurt\n5 packets (~3 tbsp) sweetener (to \ntaste)\nChocolate Strawberry \nAlmond Proteinsicles\nV E G E T A R I A N\nChocolate Strawberry Almond Proteinsicles are a delicious frozen, fruity, and chocolatey treat. They are \nEXTREMELY anabolic due to the high protein content relative to everything else (62% of the calories come \nfrom PROTEIN)! Coach Greg’s entire freezer is stuffed with these because they are delicious, anabolic, and \namazing!\nN O T E S :  P O P S I C L E T R A Y S V A R Y I N S I Z E , S O D O Y O U R \nH O M E W O R K A N D D I V I D E T H E T O T A L B A T C H C A L O R I E S \nI N T O T H E A M O U N T O F T R A Y S Y O U H A V E . S O I F T H I S \nE N T I R E B A T C H M A K E S 4 T R A Y S , T H E N D I V I D E T H E \nC A L O R I E S B Y 4 T O K N O W H O W M U C H O N E S E R V I N G I S .\nG E T C H O C O L A T E S U G A R - F R E E \nJ E L L O P U D D I N G M I X\nC L I C K T O P U R C H A S E A N I N J A \nB L E N D E R\nG E T G U A R G U M\nN U T R I T I O N\nP E R S E R V I N G\nC A L O R I E S\nF A T ( G )\nC A R B S ( G )\nF I B E R ( G )\nP R O T E I N ( G )\nB A T C H\n8 1 0\n1 2\n7 2\n1 6\n1 0 0\nP E R \nS E R V I N G\n1 9 6\n3\n1 8\n4\n2 5",
